        "description": "Today, the government has laid out their plans for new legislation in the King\u2019s speech, amid speculation that Wes Streeting is going to launch a leadership challenge against Keir Starmer as soon as Thursday. \n\nIt\u2019s rumoured that Streeting wanted to wait in order to not distract from the speech, but the rising speculation has dominated headlines and the commons.   \n\nWhat was actually in the King\u2019s speech? And what might lay ahead for the PM and the Labour party? Adam is joined by Chris and Faisal.\n\n00:00 What happened today?\n01:01 Pressure builds on the Prime Minister\n02:24 Wes Streeting\u2019s Downing Street meeting\n05:13 Market reaction to political uncertainty \n07:26 Prime Minister\u2019s defence: stability versus chaos \n09:37 State Opening of Parliament and political theatre \n13:18 What\u2019s in the King\u2019s Speech?\n17:48 Europe, Brexit and Labour\u2019s direction \n21:38 Energy, policing and terrorism laws \n26:14 What happens next in the Labour leadership race?\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://",
