        "date_published": "2026-05-13T12:43:37+00:00",
        "description": "Donald Trump has predicted that his meeting with Xi Jinping in Beijing will be \u201cvery special\u201d - but is also likely to be fraught. \n\nBoth sides are looking to stabilise the volatile China - US relationship. The talks are likely to centre on how to balance competition in trade and technology. Trump may also be seeking President Xi\u2019s help to end the war in Iran. China will feel it has the upper hand as it heads to the negotiating table with a war-weakened Washington.\n\nOur China Correspondent Laura Bicker has been to the futuristic city of Chongqing in China to explore the country\u2019s strengths and weaknesses ahead of the talks.\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#China #DonaldTrump #BBCNews",
