        "date_published": "2026-05-13T11:43:22+00:00",
        "description": "UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer is fighting to stay on in his role, despite calls from Labour critics for him to step down.\n\nAfter a disastrous set of elections for the party last week, Wes Streeting's allies have told the BBC they expect the health secretary to challenge Starmer's leadership as soon as tomorrow.\n\nFour members of his government have already resigned and many more party members are calling for him to step down.\n\nBut how did we get here? BBC Journalist Jo Crawford and BBC 5 Live\u2019s Matt Chorley explain. \n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#KeirStarmer #UKPolitics #Labour #LabourParty #BBCNews\n\n0:00 - From victory to crisis \n00:47 - Mandelson and U-turns\n02:04 - What did he achieve?\n02:33 - Who could take over?\n05:05 - Threat of Reform",
