        "description": "Twenty-two passengers and crew evacuated from a cruise ship after a hantavirus outbreak are set to leave hospital isolation in the UK.\n \nThe group, who returned from the MV Hondius expedition cruise, spent 72 hours isolating at Arrowe Park Hospital in Merseyside and will continue isolating at home for 42 days.\n \nThe UK Health Security Agency said those being monitored remain healthy and asymptomatic.\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#Hantavirus #CruiseShip #BBCNews",
